-- title:
--   The U_q Hecke set is contained in the T_q Hecke set
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the rational quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, let $N$ be a natural number, let $q$ be a prime, and let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ denotes the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Assume `IsEichlerOrder R N`, that is, $R=\Lambda_1\sqcap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ (orders maximal for inclusion among orders) with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups equal to $N$; assume further that `meetOrder R n` $=R\sqcap\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,R\,n$, where `conjByFiniteIdele R n` is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of elements of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image under $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$ lies in $n\cdot\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}\,R\cdot n^{-1}$, satisfies `IsEichlerOrder` with level $N\cdot q$. Here `finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda$ is the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime. The conclusion is the inclusion `uHeckeSet R n q` $\subseteq$ `primeHeckeSet R q`: every unit $h$ such that (i) $h$ lies in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R n) q`, i.e. $h\in$ `finiteAdeleBox (meetOrder R n)`, $q\cdot h^{-1}\in$ `finiteAdeleBox (meetOrder R n)`, $h^{-1}\notin$ `finiteAdeleBox (meetOrder R n)` and $q^{-1}\cdot h\notin$ `finiteAdeleBox (meetOrder R n)`, (ii) conjugation of `conjByFiniteIdele R n` by $h$ returns $R$, and (iii) `conjByFiniteIdele R h` $\neq$ `conjByFiniteIdele R n`, satisfies the four conditions $h\in$ `finiteAdeleBox R`, $q\cdot h^{-1}\in$ `finiteAdeleBox R`, $h^{-1}\notin$ `finiteAdeleBox R`, $q^{-1}\cdot h\notin$ `finiteAdeleBox R`.
--
--   This records that the double coset defining the operator $U_q$ on the edges of the class-set graph attached to the Eichler order of level $Nq$ is contained in the double coset defining $T_q$ on the vertices, attached to the Eichler order $R$ of level $N$. It feeds the edge–vertex compatibility of the two Hecke correspondences used in the comparison of the class-set graph with the Cerednik–Drinfeld description.
